    {
      "id": "Kclp",
      "code_hash": "844032705a78ba25d609d77b0cab77e7",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"timestamps-and-intervals\">Timestamps and intervals</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Timestamps are microseconds since 1970 (UTC) in the model; intervals are\ndurations. Comparisons with literals, <code>ts + interval</code>, <code>ts1 - ts0</code> and\njoins on time are all tracked, like integers. The calendar functions are\ncomputed exactly on the Gregorian calendar (<code>SubstraitLean/Time.lean</code>),\nand Lean proves they <strong>grow with the timestamp</strong>, so a range of\ntimestamps gives a range of years, of truncated months, and so on.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Pick a time window and see what Lean derives:</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
