          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><code>UPPER</code>, <code>LOWER</code> and regular expressions are <strong>black boxes</strong>: Lean knows\nthey return a string (or a boolean), and no proof depends on <em>which</em>\none, because Unicode case mapping and regex engines are big and\nengine-specific. A regular expression is a possible runtime error unless\nLean can see it compiles: patterns in a conservative subset of Rust's\nsyntax are accepted, anything fancier is reported. A back-reference like\n<code>\\1</code> isn't supported by DataFusion's engine at all:</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
